{
  "_comment" : [
    "CHROME ONLY.",
    "",
    "ADR-0018 CB-4: the core resolves, the shell presents. Every string here is a",
    "button label, a heading, or a statement about a PLATFORM permission — never a",
    "connection state, never a failure, never a remediation for a `reason_code`.",
    "Those come from `tw_render_diagnostic` (F-10), resolved from",
    "`contracts/registry/reason_codes.json` in the caller's locale with the",
    "next-action variant selected by `(platform, os_version)` (ADR-0019 LT-3).",
    "",
    "A string in this file that described a TwinVPN condition would be a second",
    "message catalogue outside the registry, which is R-31's defect class and the",
    "reason `twinvpnctl` rendered catalogue keys (R-15).",
    "",
    "THE `protection_*` KEYS ARE NOT AN EXCEPTION TO THAT. The protection badge",
    "is not a `Diagnostic` and has no `reason_code`: ADR-0019 \u00a711.3 lists it under",
    "'two facts ride ALONGSIDE the status', UI-2 models it as the three-valued",
    "enum `protection.indicator: PROTECTED|UNPROTECTED_ANNOUNCED|UNKNOWN`, and",
    "\u00a711.4 -- the reason-code presentation contract -- governs what a surface does",
    "with a `Diagnostic`, which this is not. Labelling a projected enum is exactly",
    "what this catalogue is for; the WHY behind a posture still arrives as a",
    "registered code (POLICY.KILLSWITCH.*, POLICY.LEAK.*) through",
    "`tw_render_diagnostic`, and that is where the family-asymmetry detail lives.",
    "",
    "These keys were previously handed to `tw_render_diagnostic` AS reason codes.",
    "`ObservedReasonCode::parse` rejects a lowercase byte, `render` degrades an",
    "unparseable code to `Domain::Internal`, and the badge -- including the",
    "PROTECTED one, next to a green shield -- read 'TwinVPN hit a defect in",
    "itself.' `Scripts/check-chrome-strings.sh` now fails on any `ui.*` literal",
    "reaching the core, so it cannot come back a third time."
  ],
  "_comment_why_a_catalogue" : [
    "WHY A CATALOGUE AND NOT SWIFT LITERALS.",
    "",
    "Not the SBOM: DP-5 (ADR-0018:1105) is one SBOM per target artifact, and this",
    "file compiles to `Localizable.strings` INSIDE the code-signed `.app`, exactly",
    "as Android's `strings.xml` compiles to `resources.arsc` inside the signed APK.",
    "A bundle resource is in the artifact by construction; a Swift literal is the",
    "thing that is not. S-46 is `CoreBuildIdentity` — which core, which ABI, which",
    "registry version — and a tab label has no registry version.",
    "",
    "The real reason is TRANSLATABILITY and ADR-0019 LT-9's pseudo-locale gate: a",
    "literal cannot be pseudo-localised, so a literal cannot be proved to survive",
    "the 40 % expansion LT-9 applies to every string."
  ],
  "_comment_key_parity" : [
    "KEY PARITY WITH ANDROID (R-36).",
    "",
    "Every key that Android already carries is spelled the SAME here, and copied",
    "from `shells/android/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml` rather than",
    "reinvented: nav_status, nav_pairing, nav_diagnostics, pairing_title,",
    "pairing_qr_description, diagnostics_title, protection_protected,",
    "protection_unprotected, protection_unknown.",
    "",
    "`protection_blocked` is the ONE key here with no Android counterpart, and it",
    "is a KNOWN PARITY GAP rather than an oversight. ADR-0019 \u00a711.9(5) gives the",
    "protection badge EXACTLY THREE values and Android carries exactly those",
    "three; `ProtectionAssertion.State` in `SupportTypes.swift` carries a fourth,",
    "`blocked`, which no contract enum defines. Rendering it as `Protected` would",
    "claim a posture, and rendering it as `Not protected` would claim a leak, so",
    "it gets \u00a711.3's own words for `BLOCKED` until the vocabulary is reconciled.",
    "",
    "`nav_status` labels the Status tab AND the Status screen's navigation title,",
    "because Android carries no separate status-screen title to copy. The three",
    "`diagnostics_*` keys below it have no Android counterpart yet: that shell has",
    "no bundle-assembly UI. They are named in Android's style so the copy runs the",
    "other way when it does."
  ],
  "sourceLanguage" : "en",
